"What about your wife?" Kate asks. "Does she hold number zero?"

"Yes," Daren says. "Though there is no zero position on the dial. Reaching her requires a coded sequence, a precaution to ensure no one dials her line by mistake."

"So," Hadrik says, "are we sure the guards will let us keep these once we are behind bars?"

"You may retain your personal effects," the royal servant says, glancing back as he guides us down the street. "Each participant is assigned an individual cell for storage, and you are permitted to keep small items on your person."

