"To you as well," Wilhelm says, turning toward his cell.

An orange-hilted blade. Specialized enchantment for dampening presence, the calling card of guild-trained assassins. I will need to watch this one closely.

}
#if(v_b2_ch2_threatened == 2) {
"Always reassuring to know I have a friend who won't bury an orange-hilted dagger between my ribs in the middle of the match," I say casually.

"Yes, it's very—" Wilhelm starts, then the words catch in his throat.

His smile hardens into confusion. "What?"

"Those enchanted blades assassins carry to hide their presence," I say. "Not that you would know anything about guild weapons, Wilhelm. Being an ordinary gladiator."

"Of course not," he says quickly.

"Fortunate for us both," I tell him, letting an icy, detached grin settle over my face in my best imitation of Eiden. "I would hate having to butcher a comrade so soon after introductions."

A thin line of sweat tracks down his temple. "Right... I am going to turn in. See you tomorrow."

"Sleep well," I call after him as he retreats toward his door.

Two can play at Eiden's detached amusement, you backstabbing bastard.

}
